nce and associate oneself with  americans who are concerned to change  these things and i don't think it's  properly framed as a racial  um as a racial problem and i certainly  don't think  that uh  you know violent  rebellion  uh gets us anywhere i i'm you know i i  get the historical  salience of that posture  and it made a lot of sense  in the early in the mid 20th century  i don't think it makes very much sense  at all in the early 21st century  you
 

